.TH SDL_HasEvents 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HasEvents \- Check for the existence of certain event types in the event queue.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_events.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_HasEvents(Uint32 minType, Uint32 maxType);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If you need to check for a single event type, use
.BR SDL_HasEvent ()
instead\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I minType
the low end of event type to be queried, inclusive; see
.BR SDL_EventType
for details\[char46]
.TP
.I maxType
the high end of event type to be queried, inclusive; see
.BR SDL_EventType
for details\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if events with type >=
.BR minType
and <=
.BR maxType
are present, or false if not\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_HasEvents (3)
